  "description": "Extend the explicit calibration action to the eleven sweepable follow-on core threshold fields.\n\n## Background\n\nThe follow-on selector migration design at `dev/active/7d824b2f/design.md` fixes the sweepability test and field set. The strict format-2 mechanism and the pilot measured core-owner envelope are inputs. This task reuses the one fresh-process steering protocol and `CoreTuningCodec`; it creates no second loader, forcing hook, or artifact representation.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: The calibration action sweeps the eleven sweepable follow-on threshold fields through the standing crossover rule. Every timed route runs in a fresh child that installs a strict prepared core section and asserts `Installed` for every steered field before public production dispatch. The parent and composer never install a profile; a nonzero exit, malformed result, `DefaultedMissing`, or `FrozenBeforeInstall` invalidates the run without publishing an artifact.\n- [hard] REQ-02: The receipt records every field's grid, timing samples and uncertainty, route observations, selection and fallback rule, and outcome—measured, tie, non-monotone, or uncalibrated—together with clean source revision, seed, host, toolchain, and separate section-measurement versus envelope-assembly provenance. A non-sweepable or invalid result remains omitted under the core codec's section-local omission rule and is never filled with an estimate.\n- [hard] REQ-03: The authoritative core-owner envelope is updated atomically and strictly reopened and contains no algebra vocabulary. Its one section-level measurement provenance and receipt cover every retained measured selector; values not covered by the run are explicitly superseded or omitted rather than copied beneath unrelated evidence.\n- [hard] REQ-04: Calibration remains an explicit action under one outer benchmark lock with no build side effect. The both-codec composer regenerates and strictly reopens the complete repository envelope while preserving the canonical core wrapper and leaving the algebra wrapper unchanged.\n",
